    {
      "type": "thinking",
      "thinking": "I'm planning the full HTML structure: a people list with unique case-insensitive validation and inline errors, an expense form with description, amount validation, payer selection, and split checkboxes defaulting to all checked, plus a newest-first expense list with removal. I'm also working out the split logic so leftover cents get distributed one each to selected people in the order they joined the trip.\n\nFor balances and settling up I'm using signed cents stored as data attributes, with a greedy debtor-creditor matching algorithm to minimize transfers, persisting everything to localStorage, formatting currency with Intl.NumberFormat in CAD, and applying Fraunces/IBM Plex Sans fonts with brand-only colors. I'm also working through careful amount validation using regex and string-based cent parsing to avoid floating point errors, along with specific inline error messages for each form field, making sure failed submissions preserve user input and checkbox states persist correctly when the people list re-renders.\n\nNow I'm thinking through the remaining details: person removal isn't required so I'll skip it, the settle-up algorithm uses sorted creditors/debtors with a two-pointer approach guaranteeing at most k-1 transactions, and I'm defining focus rings, button styles (Signal/Paper for primary, Paper/Harbour/Rope for secondary), error text styling with aria-live regions, and checkbox accent colors — then I'm ready to start writing the actual implementation.\n\n",
